+<summary>
 Explanation
 </summary>
 <p>
-<p><strong>Survival Probability (px):</strong><br> px is a vector where
-each element represents the probability of survival (1 - qx) at a
-specific age x. It starts from age 25 and continues for subsequent
-ages.<br><br></p>
-<p><strong>Subset of Survival Probabilities (px[(25 + 1):(99 +
-1)]):</strong><br> This selects p25 through p99 (positions 26 to 100),
-the one-year survival probabilities needed to get from age 25 to age
-100.<br><br></p>
-<strong>Cumulative Product Calculation (cumprod(px[(25 + 1):(99 +
-1)])):</strong><br> cumprod calculates the cumulative product of the
-selected survival probabilities. The k-th value is kp25, the probability
-that a 25-year-old survives k more years (to age 25 + k). The last value
-is the probability of reaching 100.
+<p><strong>Survival probabilities (<code>px</code>):</strong><br>
+<code>px</code> holds the one-year survival probability <span
+class="math inline">p_x = 1 - q_x</span> for each age <span
+class="math inline">x</span>.<br><br></p>
+<p><strong>Subset (<code>px[(25 + 1):(99 + 1)]</code>):</strong><br>
+This selects <span class="math inline">p_{25}</span> through <span
+class="math inline">p_{99}</span> (positions 26 to 100), the one-year
+survival probabilities needed to get from age 25 to age 100.<br><br></p>
+<strong>Cumulative product (<code>cumprod()</code>):</strong><br> The
+<span class="math inline">k</span>-th value is <span
+class="math inline">{}_kp_{25} = p_{25}\,p_{26} \cdots
+p_{25+k-1}</span>, the probability that a 25-year-old survives <span
+class="math inline">k</span> more years (to age <span
+class="math inline">25 + k</span>). The last value is the probability of
+reaching 100.
 </p>
 </details>
